  "change": "Verify that external repair of an invalid-UTF-8 selected note clears the preview error after refresh and displays the exact repaired BOM/CRLF source without vault or app-data writes.",
  "focused_test": {
    "name": "egui_refresh_after_external_invalid_utf8_note_repair_recovers_preview_without_writing",
    "command": "cargo test --workspace --locked",
    "result": "Passed on Ubuntu, macOS, and Windows GitHub Actions jobs.",
    "log_lines": {
      "ubuntu": "test tests::egui_refresh_after_external_invalid_utf8_note_repair_recovers_preview_without_writing ... ok",
      "macos": "test tests::egui_refresh_after_external_invalid_utf8_note_repair_recovers_preview_without_writing ... ok",
      "windows": "test tests::egui_refresh_after_external_invalid_utf8_note_repair_recovers_preview_without_writing ... ok"
    }
  },
  "scenario_result": [
    "Opened Notes/Welcome.md with a valid BOM/CRLF source, displayed its exact-byte preview, externally replaced it with BOM-prefixed invalid UTF-8, refreshed, and confirmed stale preview/error/receiver state cleared while the vault and selected note stayed active.",
    "A fresh preview failed closed with the explicit invalid-UTF-8 error and no source. The external repair wrote new BOM/CRLF source bytes to the same path; refresh cleared the previous error and retained the active selection.",
    "A fresh preview displayed the exact repaired bytes and full source length without truncation. Exact post-repair vault and separate app-data snapshots remained unchanged through both refreshes, failed and successful previews, and UI teardown."
  ],
